== Preface

Dear friends, I heartily commend the following discourse on closet prayer to your#super[+] serious reading. I have many reasons to hope that when you#super[+] have once read it through, you will be more in love with closet prayer than ever, that you will set a higher value on closet prayer than ever, and that you will make better and fuller use of closet prayer than you have ever yet done. Consider what I say in my epistle to the reader, and labor to use this little treatise that I now put into your#super[+] hands in such a way that God may be glorified, that your own souls may be edified, comforted, and encouraged in the ways of the Lord, and that you may be my crown and joy in the great day of our Lord Jesus (1 Thess 2:19–20). So, wishing that “the favor of Him who dwelt in the burning bush” (Deut 33:16) may rest on you#super[+] and yours forever, I take my leave and remain, dear friends, your souls’ servant in our dear Lord Jesus,

#v(1em)

